{
  "startedAt": "2026-10-18T04:12:51.820Z",
  "steps": [
    "The actual field editor converts a v1 offset track to schema2 spriteFrame2d, reviews a 2×2 grid with frame indices 0/1/3 and step sampling, and shows frame 3 in its schematic. At 390px Chinese/English/Japanese preserve the focused grid input, selection, reviewed source and footer reachability. Cancel leaves every author file and the source draft unchanged.",
    "Apply changes only the ordinary source draft. Normal Save persists exactly the reviewed animation and preserves BOM/CRLF; scene, images, registrations, templates and all other author files stay byte-identical.",
    "The saved preview freezes one shared SVG for two instances. Explicit seeks render red frame0, green frame1, yellow frame3 and loop boundary frame0 through actual nine-argument Canvas crops of the 160×160 decode. Quarter-pixel samples prove the second instance retains its complete sheet. Stop restores exact static canvas pixels and layout access.",
    "Saved-scene controls fit 390px in all three languages without losing the focused timeline or paused frame. Refresh resets to static and releases the old snapshot. Closing while a real refreshed response is held releases the late preview and cannot reopen the closed tab or retain playback."
  ],
